Subject: [PATCH] VU1 debug aids: routine counts and batch captures safe from two threads (TODO 163)

The native renderer runs the particle programs on this engine (ps2vu1fast::run, nr_particles.cpp)
from its own thread while VIF1's thread runs the game's batches. PS2X_VU1_ROUTINES' totals (a
static map, unlocked) were then changed by both threads at once: the heap corrupted, the process
ended 0xC0000374 (Cybertron at 16500 and Mid-Atlantic, both with PS2X_VU1_ROUTINES=1; never
without it). The counts now take a lock; PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE's packet list is the running thread's
own (thread_local) and its count and file numbers are taken under a lock of their own.
---
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_fast.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_fast.cpp
@@ -618,8 +618,10 @@
         e.kickBytesLog = SIZE_MAX;
     }
 
-    // The packets of the batch PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE is saving (run()), or null.
-    std::vector<uint8_t> *g_batchPackets = nullptr;
+    // The packets of the batch PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE is saving (run()), or null - the running thread's own: the native
+    // renderer runs the particle programs on this engine from its thread while VIF1's thread runs the game's batches
+    // (TODO 163).
+    thread_local std::vector<uint8_t> *g_batchPackets = nullptr;
 
     // The qword at byte `offset` of the packet as the transfer read it.
     void kickQword(const Engine &e, uint32_t offset, uint8_t out[16])
@@ -2784,6 +2786,10 @@
 
     void countRoutines(const RoutineKey &key, uint32_t vertices, uint64_t pairs, uint64_t bytes)
     {
+        // (Two threads count: VIF1's, the game's batches, and the native renderer's, its particle programs. Unlocked,
+        // the map was changed by both at once and the heap corrupted - 0xC0000374 in PS2X_VU1_ROUTINES runs, TODO 163.)
+        static std::mutex mutex;
+        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
         static std::map<RoutineKey, RoutineTotals> totals;
         static auto since = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
         RoutineTotals &entry = totals[key];
@@ -3217,6 +3223,8 @@
         if (capturing)
         {
             g_batchPackets = nullptr;
+            static std::mutex captureMutex; // (both threads may save one: the count and the file numbers)
+            std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(captureMutex);
             --batchCapture().left;
             writeBatch(e, state, batchCapture().routines, capturedPc, capturedItop, capturedTop, capturedBefore, data,
                        dataSize, code, capturedPackets);
